# A candidate projective orbit for the marked covering matrices

The vector with label zero is the twenty-sixth coordinate vector. Propagating
it along the original model's two inverse-convention generators yields these
4060 normalized vectors. The first 28 are independent, and label 658 has all
28 nonzero coordinates in that basis. These are witness data only; the action
and frame equations require separate kernel-checked certificates.

Source: ATLAS `2RuG1-f5r28B0` and `RuG1-p4060B0`; the scripts and unmodified
matrix sources are in `source/`.
-/

